47:  peq [options] [--] <target> [<path>]
51:  path                       Base directory to analyze (default: current working dir)
58:  -O, --output=OUTPUT        Output format (tree|json|dot|table|graph|mermaid)
103:Tree and table mark inferred branches `(possible)`; JSON and diagrams expose the
112:| `--output` | What it writes |
122:$ peq 'App\Domain\Invoice' src --filter=calls --output=graph
129:$ peq 'App\Domain\Invoice' src --filter=calls --output=mermaid
142:peq 'App\Domain\Invoice' src --output=dot | dot -Tsvg -o invoice.svg
164:`--output` takes the same formats as above: `graph`, `mermaid` and `dot` draw the part of the graph the answer holds, and `tree` draws the paths it bound. `--hops` sets the largest upper bound a repetition such as `{1,6}` may be written with (10 by default).
